The attached image (Figure 2) presents in vivo fluorescence imaging data illustrating the biodistribution and clearance of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles over 21 days after intramuscular injection in mice. Panel A shows that Nano-11 primarily remains localized at the injection site, with gradual decrease in signal intensity over time. Panel B confirms the absence of significant Nano-11 accumulation in major internal organs by day 21. Panel C quantitatively demonstrates the fluorescent signal's decay at the injection site, showing a rapid initial decrease followed by a moderate increase at day 2, and then steady clearance, with only about 20% of the initial signal remaining by day 21.